    <div class="main">
            <div class="area quarter ">
        <div class="container">
            <h1>
                77 to 82 % Nickel-Iron
            </h1>
        </div>
    </div>
        
    



                                    
            
                                    
    




    
    <div class="area 4rem" id="brick-0">
        <div class="container">
                    <div class="flex">
            <div class="flex anchor-wrapper">
                <h2>
                                                            
                                            <span class='subtitle'>Highest Permeability for Demanding Magnetic Sensor and Shielding Applications</span>
                                    </h2>
            </div>
        </div>
        


    




<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-6 textpic-image-container"  style="position: relative; display: inline-block;" >

                                            
                        
        
        
            
                            <figure>
                    <a href="/01_Pictures/Products/Soft%20Magnetic%20Materials%20%26%20Parts/2128/image-thumb__2128__fullImage/2006_HT_Band_11_wei%C3%9F.1b034f53.jpg" data-size="1197x798">
                        <picture >
	<source srcset="/01_Pictures/Products/Soft%20Magnetic%20Materials%20%26%20Parts/2128/image-thumb__2128__16-to-9/2006_HT_Band_11_wei%C3%9F.c27e679f.webp 1x, /01_Pictures/Products/Soft%20Magnetic%20Materials%20%26%20Parts/2128/image-thumb__2128__16-to-9/2006_HT_Band_11_wei%C3%9F@2x.c27e679f.webp 2x" width="600" height="338" type="image/webp" />
	<source srcset="/01_Pictures/Products/Soft%20Magnetic%20Materials%20%26%20Parts/2128/image-thumb__2128__16-to-9/2006_HT_Band_11_wei%C3%9F.c27e679f.jpg 1x, /01_Pictures/Products/Soft%20Magnetic%20Materials%20%26%20Parts/2128/image-thumb__2128__16-to-9/2006_HT_Band_11_wei%C3%9F@2x.c27e679f.jpg 2x" width="600" height="338" type="image/jpeg" />
	<img class="img-fluid img-textpic" src="/01_Pictures/Products/Soft%20Magnetic%20Materials%20%26%20Parts/2128/image-thumb__2128__16-to-9/2006_HT_Band_11_wei%C3%9F.c27e679f.jpg" width="600" height="338" alt="Sheets made of Nickel-Iron" title="Sheets made of Nickel-Iron" loading="lazy" srcset="/01_Pictures/Products/Soft%20Magnetic%20Materials%20%26%20Parts/2128/image-thumb__2128__16-to-9/2006_HT_Band_11_wei%C3%9F.c27e679f.jpg 1x, /01_Pictures/Products/Soft%20Magnetic%20Materials%20%26%20Parts/2128/image-thumb__2128__16-to-9/2006_HT_Band_11_wei%C3%9F@2x.c27e679f.jpg 2x" />
</picture>

                    </a>
                </figure>
            
            </div>
    <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-6">
                    <section class="wysiwyg"><p>In 77 % to 82% nickel iron alloys both the crystalline magnetic anisotropy and the magnetostriction constant approach zero, resulting in very low coercivities and highest permeabilities.<br>In other words, the materials already exhibit a significant polarization in very small external magnetic fields. Therefore 77 % to 82 % nickel iron alloys are the materials of choice for highly sensitive sensor applications (e. g. current sensors) and in particular for high quality magnetic shielding.</p>
<p><strong>Benefits:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Highest permeability leads to a very high shielding factor</li>
<li>Lowest coercivity</li>
<li>Ductile and well formable</li>
</ul></section>
                
    </div>
</div>
        </div>
    </div>

